{"id": "7a65108f-300e-4556-8df3-f19bf8240cf7", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Health checks show no open events, just upcoming lifecycle ones. Looking at metrics, I'm seeing no server errors in Bedrock's InvocationServerErrors, though I'm a bit uncertain about the dimension setup — Bedrock metrics normally key off ModelId, so querying without dimensions should return nothing, yet Invocations did return data, which is a bit odd and worth flagging as a caveat.

Since invocations did return data, the empty error metric likely means zero server errors since CloudWatch just doesn't emit when the count is zero, but this only covers server-side errors — client errors, throttling, and other paths like agents or knowledge bases aren't included. I should also note the Health API's describe_events call captures public events too, not just account-specific ones, though I still can't determine resolution time for any past issue. I notice there are two upcoming lifecycle events on 2026-11-26 marked action required, likely model deprecations, which is worth a brief mention since they're happening tomorrow rather than today.

